\f1\fs22 Rick and Dick were guys who broke into houses and placed covert listening devices and cameras\'97and occasionally, bombs and other hilarious booby traps. They undertook physical surveillance. They did nasty jobs no one else wanted.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Unfortunately, doing nasty jobs no one else wanted was far from a lucrative occupation, so they often moonlighted as ambulance punks.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Earlier, a body in the street had been reported. Rick claimed the job as Dick fired up their multi-purpose surveillance van disguised as a coronial pick-up unit. Once there, they procrastinated, knowing their shift stretched for hours yet.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91He\'92s not going anywhere,\'92 Rick said.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable> So they got meat pies and coffee, and sat in the tricked-up ambulance, taking perverse pleasure in observing the morning rush as it swirled around the man in the midnight blue suit lying as still as a statue in the street. They were hoping for some weak-stomached pedestrians to squeal, or better yet, to disgorge their breakfasts but the bustling crowd manoeuvred around the fallen figure with a practiced, professional duty of apathy. That was until a miserable cleaner with the arse out of his overalls nearly bulldozed his cart right over the deceased. When the cleaner tripped and fell on the body, Rick and Dick cackled so hard, they sprayed pie flakes and tomato sauce raining down on the ambulance\'92s dashboard.
